Consider type IIB superstring theory on the AdS_5 × S^5 background, dual to four-dimensional N=4 super Yang-Mills theory with gauge group SU(N) and 't Hooft coupling λ. Four-point correlators of single-trace half-BPS operators admit a large-N expansion whose terms can be organized as a sum over Witten diagrams in AdS_5 × S^5, and equivalently constrained by the conformal bootstrap acting on the CFT data (operator dimensions and OPE coefficients of double-trace and multi-trace operators).

Three known strategies for computing 1/N^4 (one-loop) corrections to such correlators are:
(i) the analytic conformal bootstrap, which fixes loop-level correlators by demanding consistency of the operator product expansion with crossing symmetry and using tree-level CFT data as input;
(ii) direct evaluation of one-loop Witten diagrams in AdS_5 × S^5;
(iii) integrability-based methods (such as hexagonalization and related techniques) that compute correlation functions of single-trace operators in planar and non-planar regimes from worldsheet integrability data.

Develop a unified framework that combines the analytic-bootstrap approach with either (ii) direct one-loop Witten-diagram computations or (iii) integrability-based methods, in such a way that the outputs of any two approaches give mutually consistent and mutually constraining determinations of one-loop four-point correlators of half-BPS operators in N=4 super Yang-Mills, providing nontrivial cross-checks of the CFT data (anomalous dimensions, OPE coefficients) extracted at order 1/N^4.

